> I went downstairs, found myself in the Titan's room at Medusa,

Stop, take a deep breath, and *think* before doing anything.

To the best of my knowledge, the titan is the most dangerous
NetHack monster that isn't named and unique.  (The other
possible contender is purple L, but those can be nuked
with a scroll of genocide; titans cannot.)  It's certainly the
most dangerous monster commonly encountered before
reaching Gehennom.

> took a step away from the stairs and stupidly dropped my BoH.

Ouch.  I've done things like that in NetHack before, but it's
not a recommended practice.

> I managed to escape upstairs.

Okay, that's a little better.

> Then I went back to my stack and fetched a few items which could be
> useful (the really useful stuff was in the BoH) and went down again
> with conflict. The idea was to fight my way through the small crowd
> and kill the titan.

Conflict isn't going to cut it against a Titan, for most pre-castle
characters (unless you've done an abnormally large amount of
overpreparation before getting there).

You need magic resistance bare minimum.  It's also important
to be at least fast -- very fast if possible.  Oh, and you'll want to
have reflection, because of some of the things they summon.

As for killing them, a wand of death wouldn't go amiss, if you
can somehow manage to lay your hands on one.  Failing that,
get the best ranged attack possible.  Stepping next to a titan in
order to whack it with your melee weapon isn't just dangerous,
it can also be well neigh impossible, because they tend to keep...

> However, he summoned monsters two more times before I reached him.

Yeah, that.  Titans tend to do that a lot.  It makes them hard
to kill without powerful ranged attacks.  Wands can be good,
if they're wands that magic resistance doesn't protect against.
(Wands of striking and magic missile are useless, but lightning
and fire can be effective.  Expect to use a number of charges.
[Since you have the platinum card, charges should not be a
big problem.])

